**url** `string`

One callback URL for all Caller Reputation events on this profile — business and number. See [Status callbacks](/docs/voice/concepts/caller-reputation#status-callbacks).

**method** `string`

HTTP method for the Caller Reputation callback. Allowed values: `GET`, `POST`. Defaults to `POST`.

#### Caller Reputation Behavior

Setting `enable_caller_reputation` to `true` validates the profile's business details synchronously — EIN (9 digits, US-issued), company name, full address, website, business email, and an authorized contact with an E.164 phone — and returns one `400` listing every failure if anything is missing. If validation passes, Plivo submits the business to each requested carrier network; each network resolves independently to `APPROVED` or `FAILED`. Repeating the call is a no-op for networks already registered, adds newly listed ones, and retries the failed ones.

Setting `enable_caller_reputation` to `false` deregisters the networks in `caller_reputation_carriers` (all when omitted) and stops each network's billing. The request returns a `400` if numbers are still enrolled on a network you're deregistering — disable Caller Reputation on those numbers first.

The response includes the profile's `caller_reputation_status`, `caller_reputation_by_carrier`, and `caller_reputation_updated_at` fields — see [The Profile Object](#the-profile-object) and [Caller Reputation](/docs/voice/concepts/caller-reputation) for the full status model.

