If your account is already at its concurrency limit when you call the [Make a Call API](/docs/voice/api/calls/#make-a-call), the request itself fails with HTTP status `403`. No call is created, so you get no call UUID, no hangup callback, and no entry in your call logs for that attempt. The response body carries the error message, not a numeric code:

```json theme={null}
{
  "api_id": "9e2a1c3e-4f5b-4a6c-8d7e-0f1a2b3c4d5e",
  "error": "Concurrency Limit Breached"
}
```

A call that Plivo has already accepted into your CPS queue is checked again when it is dialed. If your account has reached the limit by then, the call is dropped and appears in **Logs > Voice** with hangup cause `5030` (`Concurrency Limit Breached`), and the same code is sent to your hangup URL. Retry after a short delay once active calls have ended.

Hangup causes `5030`, `5180`, and `5190` are the same in every data region.

Call the [Update Account Phone Number](/docs/numbers/account-phone-numbers#update-an-account-phone-number) endpoint:

| Parameter | Required | Description |
| - | - | - |
| `caller_reputation` | Yes | Set to `enabled` |
| `profile_uuid` | Yes | Your business profile UUID |

The number attaches on every carrier network where your business is `APPROVED` — attachment typically completes within hours. Networks where your business is still pending, failed, or not registered are **not** attached; the response tells you why for each one, and you retry those networks by calling the same endpoint again after the business is approved.

```json theme={null}
{
  "api_id": "f31c07a2-688d-11f1-aaed-a238457c948e",
  "message": "changed",
  "caller_reputation_status": "PENDING",
  "caller_reputation_by_carrier": {
    "at&t":     { "status": "PENDING", "reason_code": null, "reason": null, "updated_at": "2026-08-20T10:02:11Z" },
    "t-mobile": { "status": "NOT_REGISTERED", "reason_code": "BUSINESS_PENDING", "reason": "Business registration on t-mobile is still pending. Retry adding this number after the business is approved.", "updated_at": "2026-08-20T10:02:11Z" },
    "verizon":  { "status": "NOT_SUPPORTED", "reason_code": "CARRIER_NOT_SUPPORTED", "reason": "Verizon is not currently supported for Caller Reputation on Plivo.", "updated_at": null }
  }
}
```

If **no** carrier network can attach — the business is pending everywhere, failed everywhere, or was never registered — the request returns a `400` naming the profile's current per-carrier state. Register or fix the business on the profile first, then retry.

